end? Well, you're not saving the world anyways.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.780
So, they're like, the stakes are like saving other worlds.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:08.400
Saving the galaxy!

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:09.980
I care about the princess.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:19.420
Yeah, we don't know if you can like, develop a loving relationship with the other life forms

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:21.920
that are in these other planets that you're saving.

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:26.440
So, yeah, you probably want to protect Princess Maria, your last chance at having any kind

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.260
of meaningful relationship with your own kind.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.300
True. What's the main character's name again?

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:34.780
N'Zal. I said nasal on purpose.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:36.480
Or nasal. To make him sound-

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:39.800
No, no, I think you're right, N'Zal, but I was trying to make him sound even weaker

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.040
because he looks weak.

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:42.200
And he is weak.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:45.700
Well, because it just sounds like, it sounds like, you know, N'Zal is like out of like a

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:49.420
science fiction thing. It just sounds like a futuristic name to me.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:51.180
Maria does not.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.600
Maria does not sound like a 5,000, your 5,012 name.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:59.520
So, I wonder if they're really just like, maybe someone thought like, oh, people today

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:02.300
in 1990 aren't going to be able to relate to this spaceman.

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:06.940
We need to give them a love interest who just sounds like a contemporary person.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:12.620
That's, you're probably right, but I think they could have just done the half measure

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:14.800
and called her like, Mariax.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.900
Mariax sounds like a split between the two.

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:23.240
You know, Joe, they did the same thing in Sonic Adventure 2 Battle where Shadow the Hedgehog

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:26.780
is in love with Maria and he wants to save Maria.

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:32.780
So, he has to team up with Sonic the Hedgehog in order to save Maria.

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:36.940
Interesting. Yeah, maybe it's just an all West Side Story thing.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.100
Maria is a human.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.540
Thank you for checking on that.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:44.400
They definitely keep doing that and it makes me feel very strange about Sonic.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:50.020
Can you guys think of any other games where you fight from inside a monster?

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:52.720
Yeah, haven't we had like several shmups?

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:57.240
I mean, to answer your question, no, I can't think of any, but haven't we had multiple shmups

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.820
where you fight inside like an organic thing?

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:01.580
Life Force comes to mind.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:05.900
Life Force. The final stage of Life Force, you actually have to go inside, which is cool.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:13.240
It's a trope as like a gimmick level or not like a gimmick, but it's definitely a theme

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:21.240
that will show up in a game, but never the focal point of like the aesthetic of a game.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:28.080
Like this is, I was very surprised by the visual design of this game.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:33.360
Yeah, we should probably talk about that too, because all of the creatures in the game, and

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:38.480
I'm using them creatures instead of enemies, they're all pretty like gruesome by eight pit

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:39.680
pixel standards.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:44.180
Like there's, you know, where you would usually get in a Gradius style game, like similar style

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:47.060
spaceships flying at you that you have to shoot down.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:49.120
Instead, you get flying eyeballs.

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:52.880
You know, like that's, that's the first thing you see on the screen.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.520
You're like, whoa, this is pretty heavy.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:58.420
Yeah. It's got some like body horror vibes.

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:01.120
Like I kept thinking of Existence.

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:03.300
I don't know if you guys saw that movie.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:14.620
It was like a Cronenberg movie, but it was, there was this piece of electronics that it was

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:18.800
like a virtual reality video game, but it got like way too organic.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:25.180
And there was a lot of weird like merging of body and technology.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:26.700
And it was super gruesome.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:28.620
That's definitely a Cronenberg thing.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:35.720
Yeah. I mean, everything in this, like even the walls and like the surroundings is all very

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:42.120
organic and, and, you know, it feels very squishy, you know, to the point where like,

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:46.980
like, I mean, there's a, there's a level that looks to me like you're just flying through

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.960
a bunch of like intestines.

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:56.480
And then there are like parts where you have like this fleshy membrane are the walls.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:19:01.580
And like suddenly that membrane turns into these like grotesque hands that come out and grab

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:06.600
at you. And like, it is like, it's, it's definitely like trying to emulate this.

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:10.560
Yeah. I mean, Cronenberg is a good, good thought, but yeah, it's like trying to do like this body horror

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:12.420
feel to it.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:20.420
Yeah. And there's something about, you know, like NES graphics at the time were the best graphics

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:22.500
that you had outside of like the arcades and stuff.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:27.360
So for people like, you know, it could have seemed very real or whatever in the same way

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:31.500
that like now I make fun of, you know, N64 and PS1 graphics.

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:37.200
But when I was a kid, the piano with teeth in Super Mario 64, like scared the shit out

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.400
of me, like legitimately terrified me.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:45.880
I feel like the first boss in this game is something that a young me would have like shut

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:50.860
the game off in fear of because I'm not quite sure what happened to that cow.

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:55.700
Uh, I'm assuming it's a cow, but it's also like a skeleton cow with its brain still like

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:57.020
intact to it.

00:19:57.580 --> 00:20:00.900
And, uh, I saw of it more of like a horse dog.

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.460
Okay. I thought it was a wolf.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:03.880
I don't know.

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:08.540
Yeah. I guess I see wolf more than any of these, but it also looks like there's like something

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:09.580
else attached to it.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:12.980
Like it has like another, it has a third eye like leached onto it.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:16.860
So it's like the skeleton of a, uh, of a wolf.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:23.780
But then like the parasitis has like leached itself onto it and is just like, it's the

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:28.980
actual brains and the skeleton is just like being reanimated by the parasite.

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:35.180
I see. Talk about like what really like one, like bosses that freaked that are freaky.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:39.780
A few bosses later, I think it's like, I mean, there's a lot of like mini bosses and

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:44.040
stuff too. So I don't know which one you'd consider it, but it's like maybe stage five or something.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:52.400
There's that like thing that it's like, it's like a giant humanoid red gross man who out

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:57.780
of his chest is an eyeball and like his head, his head curves around to the top of the screen.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:00.340
He's looking down on you as you're like fighting it.

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:05.920
Like it's hard to describe, but it is that is to me was like the most like unsettling boss.

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:08.360
Yeah, there's, there's those kinds of bosses.

00:21:08.380 --> 00:21:13.080
And then at some point you get like a fish with a helmet, which is a little less scary,

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:17.440
but overall like very unique boss designs.

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:24.720
Yeah. Even the ones that are following the, uh, you know, the greatest like shoot the core style

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:28.840
where it's like, there's an eyeball, um, that you just have to keep hitting as the weak

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:35.580
point. That's like, yeah, there's a gigantic eyeball and it's attached to a, like, you know, a

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:36.800
person's chest or whatever.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:39.360
It's like, that's, it's like, why'd you have to go the extra distance?

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:40.520
Like, just give me the eyeball.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:42.460
Like that's scary enough to shoot at.

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:45.280
Now you're like, you know, it's coming out of somebody's chest.

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:52.480
Like that's insane. And I think one that, uh, I think this, we're talking about a different one.

00:21:52.640 --> 00:22:01.320
It's in one of the vertical levels, um, where you're going through the, the intestine sort

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:02.600
of feeling area.

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:09.120
And then it's, you, you end up getting split into two paths and it seems like a separate

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:13.140
objects, but it's still a part of the background.

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:18.380
And you see like, like teeth kind of coming out and blocking your way.

00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:20.760
It's like a bit of a timing mini game there.

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:28.100
And then at the end you see this weird parasite looking thing.

00:22:28.100 --> 00:22:33.880
So it just looks like, you know, a typical parasite that you might have if you ate some

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:36.560
eight year old egg or something.

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:42.620
And that was just the fact that it really committed to it and not so much like, oh, how,

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:46.800
uh, how fucked up can we try and look?

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:49.540
And it looked a little bit more like something that could exist.

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:51.440
That one was pretty intense.

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:56.320
Yeah. That's a really cool one because it's all like you were saying, like, it's not revealed to

00:22:56.320 --> 00:22:59.100
be the boss when you're going down the corridors.

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:04.900
So, uh, then you realize like the scale of the enemy to like the size of it.

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:07.240
And granted, you don't have to take it all down or anything.

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:08.980
Um, it doesn't, didn't start moving.

00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:11.700
You just shoot the, um, the end point.

00:23:11.780 --> 00:23:17.860
But like, I really appreciate just not even the commitment to the design or anything, but

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:24.400
like, you know, we don't see this even, even in like the sci-fi futuristic games that

00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:27.160
we get like, um, that are greatest spinoffs.

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:34.260
Otherwise like this commits completely to the idea of gross body horror, uh, your inside

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:38.880
of a living planet thing in a way that also like completely works for shmups, you know,

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:44.700
like everything that shoots projectiles and, um, whether they're attached to the environment

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:48.800
or as individual enemies, like there's nothing that shows up here.

00:23:48.920 --> 00:23:54.560
That's too weird. Other than those like pterodactyls at the beginning, I'm not sure what the point of them was, but

00:23:54.560 --> 00:23:56.240
everything else fits right in.

00:23:57.260 --> 00:24:02.120
Uh, going a little bit into the, the actual gameplay design.

00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:09.460
I really appreciated how, you know, you've got a unique perspective here because yes, it's

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:15.560
one of those shmups that'll change between, uh, vertical and horizontal, but the vertical

00:24:16.210 --> 00:24:17.380
it's going down.

00:24:17.520 --> 00:24:20.020
And that, that's something that we haven't seen before.

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:25.180
And in any other context, it'd be like, why did they do this?

00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:31.580
Like there are conventions for a reason, but then you realize like what it's doing and it

00:24:31.580 --> 00:24:37.860
has that commitment to the aesthetic, uh, that you would be going down if you're going through

00:24:37.860 --> 00:24:45.620
the, the like digestive system of a planet size, disgusting parasite.

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:49.640
So I really appreciated that aspect of the design.

00:24:49.980 --> 00:24:56.680
Yeah. And I don't know if this was intentional, but to that same point, like going down, going

00:24:56.680 --> 00:25:02.260
top down in a shmup like this just feels like, at least to us, cause we've played other, so

00:25:02.260 --> 00:25:07.140
many other shmups and just games in general, it feels a little off.

00:25:07.140 --> 00:25:08.380
It feels like unsettling.

00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:13.740
Like I think it helps add to that feel of like unpredictability or like something's wrong.

00:25:13.980 --> 00:25:18.860
Well, the whole game too, isn't one that lets you explore much.

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:22.200
Uh, not that it, not that the rails move fast or anything.

00:25:22.200 --> 00:25:23.340
It is a shmup on rails.

00:25:23.480 --> 00:25:28.140
So you're waiting for the scrolling to happen, but it's just that the, the space that they

00:25:28.140 --> 00:25:30.260
lock for you isn't very much.

00:25:30.360 --> 00:25:35.980
And if anything, it just continues to get like tighter and tighter, the further you go into

00:25:35.980 --> 00:25:42.040
the levels. And so that kind of creates both a claustrophobic feeling of like no turning back, but also

00:25:42.040 --> 00:25:49.780
from a, from a gameplay stand of view, there's like, it's really interesting how in other games, like

00:25:49.780 --> 00:25:55.420
platformers, for instance, sometimes we complain about like how, how, uh, closed in the levels

00:25:55.420 --> 00:25:59.080
are and the lack of freedom in the jump and stuff like that here.

00:25:59.080 --> 00:26:04.080
Sure. My, my initial thought might've been to say like, oh, it's really like weird that they

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:10.120
don't let you roam around, uh, this, uh, you know, this alien creature, but it works.

00:26:10.140 --> 00:26:14.060
And it also doesn't make the game significantly more challenging by closing you in.

00:26:14.160 --> 00:26:17.660
If anything, you have to play those tight corners like appropriately.

00:26:17.660 --> 00:26:23.740
So those teeth that, uh, that keep spawning out, you know, um, they're like fangs.

00:26:24.040 --> 00:26:28.560
Uh, that's very interesting that it's just a timing thing.

00:26:28.560 --> 00:26:30.400
It doesn't make the game necessarily any harder.

00:26:30.600 --> 00:26:36.320
You just wait to go around them and everything, but you're kind of locked off and, um, and you're

00:26:36.320 --> 00:26:39.800
dealing with only like a particular, uh, enemy at that point.

00:26:39.920 --> 00:26:42.780
There's, there's not like an enemy overloaded any particular instance.

00:26:42.940 --> 00:26:48.560
It's just that most of the enemies require, uh, you know, some form of thought.

00:26:48.700 --> 00:26:51.020
You can't just, uh, dodge the bullets.

00:27:28.360 --> 00:27:29.800
it can get away with that.

00:27:30.060 --> 00:27:31.420
If it were any other,

00:27:31.420 --> 00:27:32.320
like, you know,

00:27:32.460 --> 00:27:33.960
boilerplate, uh,

00:27:34.440 --> 00:27:35.800
shmup game, I might say like,

00:27:35.880 --> 00:27:37.840
Hey, that's interesting that they at least did something different,

00:27:37.840 --> 00:27:39.800
but that's sort of like a rule you don't break.

00:27:39.900 --> 00:27:42.640
Like give the player space to move around.

00:27:42.760 --> 00:27:43.920
If this is going to be a bullet hell,

00:27:44.040 --> 00:27:47.660
but because of the theme and the context,

00:27:47.660 --> 00:27:49.500
it does make sense.

00:27:49.720 --> 00:27:54.320
Uh, but I will say that those sort of timing,

00:27:54.960 --> 00:28:02.260
uh, navigational challenges are kind of the least of your concerns when it comes to the difficulty of this game.

00:28:03.040 --> 00:28:04.040
Yeah, I think it,

00:28:04.080 --> 00:28:05.480
it does play into the,

00:28:05.560 --> 00:28:06.960
like how you approach,

00:28:07.660 --> 00:28:09.220
how you approach the game in general,

00:28:09.220 --> 00:28:10.980
because for me,

00:28:11.120 --> 00:28:12.140
a lot of times in a shmup,

00:28:12.820 --> 00:28:15.020
just being not particularly great at them,

00:28:15.600 --> 00:28:19.760
I like my method or my strategy will be like to try and get past a lot of enemies.

00:28:19.860 --> 00:28:22.760
Cause I know I'm not gonna be able to like dodge their fire for long or,

00:28:22.760 --> 00:28:23.760
or take them all out.

00:28:24.060 --> 00:28:25.060
And so I was,

00:28:25.180 --> 00:28:30.680
you know, kind of trying to stay close to the front of the screen without getting surprised by things that I can't see.

00:28:30.900 --> 00:28:40.120
But I did over time kind of realize like this game really felt to me like it was encouraging me to hang back and like manage what's ahead of me.

00:28:40.480 --> 00:28:42.220
Because you,

00:28:42.220 --> 00:28:43.760
you don't have a lot of places,

00:28:44.120 --> 00:28:50.480
space to move. So like when you go forward and there's a bunch of like quote unquote turrets or whatever you'd call the equivalent,

00:28:50.480 --> 00:28:53.060
the organic equivalent of these turrets around,

00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:54.900
like you're going to get trapped in,

00:28:54.980 --> 00:28:56.620
in just like a web of,

00:28:56.620 --> 00:28:59.260
of projectiles that you can't like escape from.

00:28:59.540 --> 00:29:00.780
So like,

00:29:00.860 --> 00:29:03.280
I actually found over time,

00:29:03.280 --> 00:29:05.120
I started using these like obstacles,

00:29:05.140 --> 00:29:11.060
like those teeth coming out or like other things that were blocking my way for a moment.

00:29:11.060 --> 00:29:13.660
Like, like as a reminder to like,

00:29:13.740 --> 00:29:16.460
okay, I can hang back here and shoot things ahead,

00:29:17.260 --> 00:29:24.160
you know, while I'm like kind of both waiting for my opportunity to move as well as like making it safer to move.

00:29:24.740 --> 00:29:26.920
Um, so I felt like a lot of other,

00:29:26.920 --> 00:29:33.160
a lot of other shmups have like encouraged me just being like as aggressive and twitchy as possible.

00:29:33.500 --> 00:29:39.600
Whereas this kind of like made me like for the most as you can in a shmup that is auto scrolling.

00:29:39.980 --> 00:29:42.940
It made me want to like sit back and think.

00:29:43.640 --> 00:29:45.160
Yeah, I think the worst,

00:29:45.400 --> 00:29:49.320
uh, part of the game in terms of the claustrophobic,

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:53.960
uh, tight spaces is that it does kind of break that rule at times.

00:29:54.160 --> 00:29:56.540
With the design where certain things,

00:29:56.760 --> 00:30:02.060
um, that stand in your way are designed to be shot at in order to clear them out.

00:30:02.180 --> 00:30:05.140
You know, you're like shooting out the intestines and then it,

00:30:05.180 --> 00:30:06.900
uh, creates a hole that you go through.

00:30:07.060 --> 00:30:08.240
And then there are other,

00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:12.180
uh, design elements in this game that are designed to be like,

00:30:12.320 --> 00:30:13.460
oh no, that's like in,

00:30:13.660 --> 00:30:17.140
that's in the foreground and you go through them and you might not know that,

00:30:17.140 --> 00:30:18.700
uh, the first time you play through this.

00:30:18.780 --> 00:30:19.800
And so you're shooting at it,

00:30:19.940 --> 00:30:21.380
waiting for, uh,

00:30:21.620 --> 00:30:22.740
it to destroy.

00:30:22.740 --> 00:30:24.340
And most likely the,

00:30:24.340 --> 00:30:28.340
the sign would come up immediately that your bullets are going through it.

00:30:28.440 --> 00:30:30.200
So you too can also go through it.

00:30:30.260 --> 00:30:32.500
But in a game where like everything counts,

00:30:32.520 --> 00:30:34.620
it is kind of weird that they like,

00:30:35.220 --> 00:30:38.460
they set it up two different ways without having two different kinds of looks.

00:30:38.600 --> 00:30:41.540
There's obviously no like way to do a transparency,

00:30:42.360 --> 00:30:44.420
uh, with the foreground and the background.

00:30:44.920 --> 00:30:49.720
Yeah. There were a couple of times where those things you're talking about literally were the exact same,

00:30:49.720 --> 00:30:51.920
like tile set as this,

00:30:52.040 --> 00:30:53.280
as the walls.

00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:54.360
So it was like,

00:30:54.440 --> 00:30:55.820
okay, this looks like more wall,

00:30:55.960 --> 00:30:57.180
but it's just not.

00:30:58.360 --> 00:31:01.000
One other last thing on the,

00:31:01.000 --> 00:31:03.720
uh, the navigation challenges.

00:31:03.940 --> 00:31:05.320
Uh, it,

00:31:05.400 --> 00:31:06.660
it also, again,

00:31:06.740 --> 00:31:08.540
I don't know how intentional this was,

00:31:08.540 --> 00:31:09.780
or if this was just like,

00:31:09.900 --> 00:31:12.820
Oh, you know, most shmups have speed upgrades,

00:31:13.060 --> 00:31:14.400
but if you get too many of those,

00:31:14.560 --> 00:31:20.180
you're probably just going to run wild and very poorly perform them.

00:31:20.340 --> 00:31:21.280
Cause I, you,

00:31:21.280 --> 00:31:22.880
you end up getting super twitchy.

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:26.260
If you get too many speed upgrades and you just run right into the wall.

00:31:26.740 --> 00:31:28.440
Yeah. It's funny with any shmup that,

00:31:28.440 --> 00:31:32.040
that gets to that level where you're trying to now avoid power-ups.

00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:33.220
I definitely know what you're talking about,

00:31:33.280 --> 00:31:40.780
Sean. And I tried to avoid anything beyond two speed power-ups because I was most likely just going to twitch my way into a wall on accident.

00:31:41.060 --> 00:31:42.080
But, uh,

00:31:42.180 --> 00:31:44.460
in other shmups, that's also kind of a thing where,

00:31:45.080 --> 00:31:47.840
uh, you know, if you collect one kind of power-up,

00:31:48.220 --> 00:31:49.880
if you collect a different kind of power-up,

00:31:49.960 --> 00:31:51.820
now you lost the old power-up.

00:31:51.900 --> 00:31:53.940
And so you have to dodge those sometimes too.

00:31:54.060 --> 00:31:55.300
And I, and I don't like that.

00:31:55.440 --> 00:31:57.520
And this game doesn't make that mistake where,

00:31:58.000 --> 00:31:59.940
uh, you know, Oh, you can only have one type of power-up.

00:32:00.040 --> 00:32:02.460
Like you can collect all of the types of power-ups.

00:32:02.460 --> 00:32:07.840
And I do think that the game does a good job of at least while you retain all your power-ups,

00:32:07.920 --> 00:32:09.560
you know, the thing before you die,

00:32:10.020 --> 00:32:11.480
um, while you have them all,

00:32:11.640 --> 00:32:14.580
it does a good job of making you feel really strong.

00:32:14.820 --> 00:32:22.720
And like, you can take care of what's in front of you because you're getting all different kinds of projectiles and homing missiles and shields.

00:32:22.900 --> 00:32:23.740
And, you know,

00:32:23.760 --> 00:32:25.140
it's not just like one of each two.

00:32:25.260 --> 00:32:27.000
Like you're, you're moving along.

00:32:27.380 --> 00:32:28.940
It's just that the issue is,

00:32:29.040 --> 00:32:31.300
as you mentioned, because the game is so hard,

00:32:31.300 --> 00:32:33.300
it's, it's a one hit kill.

00:32:33.520 --> 00:32:36.960
You lose all your power-ups and you restart from a checkpoint.

00:32:37.160 --> 00:32:40.920
You don't even just like immediately spawn back in with your ship.

00:32:41.440 --> 00:32:43.420
So there's a lot to ask.

00:32:43.580 --> 00:32:44.540
Yeah. Well,

00:32:44.660 --> 00:32:47.800
there are several different kinds of power-ups that can stack.

00:32:48.060 --> 00:32:50.820
Your base fire can get overwritten.

00:32:50.820 --> 00:32:54.200
Overwritten. So I was also avoiding certain,

00:32:54.300 --> 00:32:56.520
those are like the different shaped pickups.

00:32:57.000 --> 00:32:59.920
Um, I know a lot of them have just a letter on them,

00:33:00.060 --> 00:33:02.520
like we're picking up the bombs or not bombs.

00:33:02.760 --> 00:33:05.180
The things that orbit you are their own thing.

00:33:05.180 --> 00:33:06.840
And then there's a missile category.

00:33:06.840 --> 00:33:08.460
And then there's the speed ones.

00:33:08.620 --> 00:33:10.320
And then there's your base fire,

00:33:10.460 --> 00:33:14.460
which can be any number of different spreads or projectile shapes.

00:33:14.840 --> 00:33:17.300
Um, and those can mess you up.

00:33:17.480 --> 00:33:20.260
If you found one that you really jive with and,

00:33:20.260 --> 00:33:23.880
uh, you go back to just a,

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:25.620
a straight shot,

00:33:25.620 --> 00:33:26.940
which can really mess with you.

00:33:27.180 --> 00:33:28.340
Yeah. I noticed that too.

00:33:28.420 --> 00:33:31.180
There's one I particularly liked was just like a giant bubble.

00:33:31.540 --> 00:33:33.000
And every time I was a little sad,

00:33:33.140 --> 00:33:34.020
I would be a little disappointed.

00:33:35.220 --> 00:33:36.900
But as hard as the game is,

00:33:37.140 --> 00:33:39.520
especially with the reset of power-ups,

00:33:39.620 --> 00:33:40.560
which I'm sure we'll get into,

00:33:40.740 --> 00:33:42.540
which we have talked about in other shmups too.

00:33:42.900 --> 00:33:44.380
Um, there is an interesting,

00:33:44.580 --> 00:33:48.360
uh, continue forever standpoint that the game takes as well,

00:33:48.440 --> 00:33:52.000
where, uh, no matter how many game overs you get,

00:33:52.020 --> 00:33:56.280
you do get to just continue from at least the stage that you were on,

00:33:56.380 --> 00:33:57.220
not from the checkpoint,

00:33:57.440 --> 00:33:58.860
but from the stage you were on.

00:33:59.060 --> 00:34:00.540
So there is a way to,

00:34:00.540 --> 00:34:01.360
uh, um,

00:34:02.140 --> 00:34:05.300
if you can figure out a way to rebuild up your power-ups and,

00:34:05.300 --> 00:34:06.940
and learn the level properly,

00:34:07.400 --> 00:34:10.220
you at least don't have to start over from level one.

00:34:10.500 --> 00:34:11.640
Uh, a nice,

00:34:11.920 --> 00:34:13.760
um, consolation prize,

00:34:13.920 --> 00:34:18.120
if you will, because it is very hard when you lose all your power-ups to gain them back.

00:34:18.280 --> 00:34:19.320
So we're, it's all,

00:34:19.400 --> 00:34:20.740
we're dealing in theoreticals here,

00:34:20.900 --> 00:34:22.500
but I do think that the,

00:34:22.700 --> 00:34:31.040
uh, continue from the start of the stage you died in makes more sense from a player progression standpoint than starting all the way over.

00:34:31.900 --> 00:34:33.460
Yeah. I mean, losing your,

00:34:34.380 --> 00:34:36.800
losing your power-ups is punishment enough.

00:34:37.100 --> 00:34:38.240
I, in my opinion,

00:34:38.420 --> 00:34:40.420
where like, I feel like a lot of games will tend to overdo it.

00:34:40.480 --> 00:34:41.760
Be like, yeah, you lose your power-ups.

00:34:41.760 --> 00:34:42.740
And then if you die three times,

00:34:42.800 --> 00:34:43.800
you start the whole game over.

00:34:44.520 --> 00:34:47.580
I think that that, at this day and age,

00:34:47.640 --> 00:34:49.920
I feel like that just encourages people to be like,

00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:50.960
okay, I'm done with this game.

00:34:51.720 --> 00:34:53.420
Going inside of a body,

00:34:53.820 --> 00:34:54.980
of any kind of body,

00:34:54.980 --> 00:34:57.920
um, this being an alien body.

00:34:58.080 --> 00:35:03.580
Like, there could have been another way to play this where this game is more like silly and cute and all that.

00:35:03.820 --> 00:35:06.700
Um, you know, being like playful to the idea of like,

00:35:06.760 --> 00:35:08.060
now you're in, uh,

00:35:08.200 --> 00:35:09.960
this organ or now you're in the,

00:35:10.060 --> 00:35:11.100
you know, this. It's like,

00:35:11.160 --> 00:35:12.320
it's like magic school bus.

00:35:12.540 --> 00:35:13.660
Yeah, exactly. Exactly.

00:35:13.880 --> 00:35:16.140
Or that episode of the rug rats where they go inside Chucky.

00:35:16.420 --> 00:35:17.420
Um, yeah, the,

00:35:17.920 --> 00:35:19.040
yeah, the watermelon seed,

00:35:19.120 --> 00:35:19.960
the, the idea here though,

00:35:19.960 --> 00:35:21.000
I guess what I'm saying is like,

00:35:21.220 --> 00:35:28.100
it does take a turn as it should where like all of a sudden now there's like computer components and,

00:35:28.560 --> 00:35:30.360
you know, other aliens with,

00:35:30.360 --> 00:35:34.060
with guns and stuff like towards the end of the game.

00:35:35.140 --> 00:35:36.740
I'm not saying that that's a bad thing.

00:35:36.840 --> 00:35:38.500
I'm saying like it could have gone either way.

00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:40.900
And I'm just more interested on like,

00:35:41.040 --> 00:35:42.420
uh, you know,

00:35:42.560 --> 00:35:45.140
from a, from a going inside the body POV,

00:35:45.420 --> 00:35:46.720
where do you guys stand on that?

00:35:47.820 --> 00:35:49.100
Where do I stand?

00:35:49.100 --> 00:35:52.400
I don't understand the fact that there's like guns in the body.

00:35:52.580 --> 00:35:53.460
No, or like, you know,

00:35:53.540 --> 00:35:55.720
that they didn't commit completely to the,

00:35:55.720 --> 00:35:58.520
um, navigating inside of,

00:35:58.640 --> 00:35:59.680
of a body. And instead,

00:35:59.720 --> 00:36:02.720
then it becomes more like this sci-fi technology.

00:36:02.880 --> 00:36:04.760
Like you're fighting a robot.

00:36:04.880 --> 00:36:06.080
And then there's like,

00:36:06.140 --> 00:36:12.780
you know, a whole, like it loses the whole like guts and intestinal thing and starts becoming more like,

00:36:12.900 --> 00:36:19.040
it starts to look at least a little bit more like a traditional sci-fi game where you're,

00:36:19.100 --> 00:36:21.620
like inside another spaceship.

00:36:21.980 --> 00:36:23.540
Yeah. I, I guess I,

00:36:23.820 --> 00:36:28.720
I will grant that it definitely isn't just intestines the whole time,

00:36:28.720 --> 00:36:31.360
but there is always kind of a,

00:36:31.360 --> 00:36:32.320
uh,

00:36:32.740 --> 00:36:37.460
dark aspect to whatever situation you're in.

00:36:37.460 --> 00:36:38.900
And you can like,

00:36:39.100 --> 00:36:40.720
even the ones that,

00:36:40.720 --> 00:36:41.800
that,

00:36:41.920 --> 00:36:47.880
uh, that sort of get away from that visceral feel are still like,

00:36:47.960 --> 00:36:49.120
Oh, that could be bone.

00:36:49.120 --> 00:36:53.240
And it still looks like there's just weird worms everywhere.

00:36:53.240 --> 00:36:54.980
It's always disgusting.

00:36:55.500 --> 00:36:59.320
Unless you are in a section that has more technology,

00:36:59.320 --> 00:37:02.900
but I still think that that sort of fits with the aesthetic because,

00:37:02.900 --> 00:37:03.900
you know,

00:37:04.340 --> 00:37:06.600
Star Trek Borg kind of thing.

00:37:06.840 --> 00:37:08.020
Like, I,

00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:10.860
I think that they committed as much as they should have.

00:37:11.280 --> 00:37:12.660
Yeah. I, I'm not like,

00:37:12.820 --> 00:37:14.940
I'm not against it.

00:37:14.960 --> 00:37:15.900
I think that it,

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:16.940
I think that it's like,

00:37:17.300 --> 00:37:20.380
you know, it leads to like an interesting thoughts of like,

00:37:20.440 --> 00:37:23.420
okay, so like this is disorganic thing that,

00:37:23.900 --> 00:37:29.080
you know, something or someone is building onto it or maybe it's capable of technology or

00:37:29.080 --> 00:37:31.280
it's merged with some sort of technology or whatever.

00:37:31.940 --> 00:37:33.140
Um, yeah, the part that I'm,

00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:36.720
I didn't, I didn't get very far in cause I did not beat this game,

00:37:36.760 --> 00:37:41.240
but the part that I'm like watching right now is definitely like tech,

00:37:41.400 --> 00:37:44.480
you know, there's like laser beams and like light bulbs and,

00:37:44.920 --> 00:37:46.020
you know, things like that.

00:37:46.120 --> 00:37:47.420
And I, I think that that's interesting.

00:37:47.560 --> 00:37:51.840
Maybe they just thought that the purely organic stuff would get stale or like

00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:54.280
they kind of started out of the gate with this dark,

00:37:54.460 --> 00:37:55.680
purely organic,

00:37:55.880 --> 00:37:59.360
like gross level of like design.

00:37:59.900 --> 00:38:00.780
So maybe they're like,

00:38:00.840 --> 00:38:01.700
well, where do we go? Like,

00:38:01.880 --> 00:38:02.860
what's the next thing?

00:38:02.980 --> 00:38:03.960
That's like the final thing.

00:38:04.100 --> 00:38:05.500
We like got to add something new.

00:38:05.880 --> 00:38:10.640
So tech combined with the grossness is where it ends up.

00:38:49.660 --> 00:38:51.560
And at the very end of the game,

00:38:51.560 --> 00:38:54.200
another thing that is similar to life force,

00:38:54.480 --> 00:38:56.900
uh, is that after you defeated,

00:38:56.920 --> 00:38:57.740
uh,

00:38:57.800 --> 00:39:00.060
the final boss, you have to escape,

00:39:00.540 --> 00:39:04.300
uh, from it. And that becomes a twitch reflex.

00:39:04.420 --> 00:39:06.140
Like, make sure that you,

00:39:06.380 --> 00:39:10.200
uh, don't hit any of these walls that are just randomly placed all over the place.

00:39:10.560 --> 00:39:14.760
Um, and squeeze through these little hallways before the exit.

00:39:14.760 --> 00:39:16.900
And it goes on for a pretty long time.

00:39:17.280 --> 00:39:19.580
Um, I'm just not sure like how much of that,

00:39:19.880 --> 00:39:27.240
like, is that a good ending for a shmup where the whole point of the game otherwise was to,

00:39:27.620 --> 00:39:29.040
you know, as they say,

00:39:29.400 --> 00:39:32.460
shoot up all the enemies and take down all the bosses.

00:39:32.460 --> 00:39:36.640
Is it weird that the final challenge is just this like fast reflexes?

00:39:37.260 --> 00:39:41.080
Like the screen is scrolling faster than it ever did during the regular game.

00:39:41.080 --> 00:39:45.240
And one bad movement will destroy you.

00:39:45.460 --> 00:39:46.280
Like it seems,

00:39:46.280 --> 00:39:47.240
seems misplaced.

00:39:47.400 --> 00:39:48.740
I think it works.

00:39:49.060 --> 00:39:51.740
Um, I mean, I didn't get to this point because again,

00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:53.520
the game is very difficult.

00:39:54.020 --> 00:39:57.180
Um, but in terms of a,

00:39:57.180 --> 00:40:00.580
a sort of change in the gameplay loop,

00:40:00.640 --> 00:40:01.540
uh,

00:40:01.900 --> 00:40:05.620
to hammer home that this is the close.

00:40:05.800 --> 00:40:06.660
This is the climax.

00:40:06.660 --> 00:40:08.660
This is the great escape.

00:40:08.660 --> 00:40:09.820
I think it works.

00:40:10.240 --> 00:40:13.620
Um, I haven't experienced it,

00:40:13.640 --> 00:40:26.620
but in theory, I guess I can see that like for that to be the like final challenge without that ever being like a smaller version of the challenge throughout the game.

00:40:26.620 --> 00:40:29.320
Like, it's not like the game isn't giving you like,

00:40:29.380 --> 00:40:31.040
okay, now use what we taught you.

00:40:31.220 --> 00:40:32.900
It's like now learn this new thing.

00:40:33.580 --> 00:40:34.540
So to that point,

00:40:34.560 --> 00:40:36.820
I kind of understand like if,

00:40:36.820 --> 00:40:38.320
if people would complain about that,

00:40:38.360 --> 00:40:39.720
like, I don't know,

00:40:39.820 --> 00:40:41.980
maybe if there were other times where you had to dodge things,

00:40:42.000 --> 00:40:43.800
like, I know you have to do that the whole game,

00:40:43.820 --> 00:40:49.060
but like not at this speed and not like strictly like this is clearly an obstacle course and not,

00:40:49.520 --> 00:40:51.200
uh, like fight enemies anymore.

00:40:51.500 --> 00:40:54.460
And like, there was no other part of the game that was like that.

00:40:55.020 --> 00:40:56.780
So it feels a little like,

00:40:57.420 --> 00:40:58.960
wait, where the heck did this come from?

00:40:59.120 --> 00:41:00.060
But, uh,

00:41:00.240 --> 00:41:01.700
I'm kind of neutral on it.

00:41:02.020 --> 00:41:03.460
Just to defend it one last time.

00:41:03.600 --> 00:41:08.660
Like, okay, if you're going to make me get eaten at the beginning of the game,

00:41:09.820 --> 00:41:12.480
I'm sure as hell going to expect you to poop me out.

00:41:13.420 --> 00:41:14.900
So that's where I feel.

00:41:14.900 --> 00:41:16.940
And I think thematically they,

00:41:16.940 --> 00:41:18.320
they kept their promise.

00:41:18.620 --> 00:41:21.100
I, I see both sides.

00:41:21.100 --> 00:41:22.340
Uh, and I understand,

00:41:22.540 --> 00:41:24.380
you know, that like it spices it up,

00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:26.920
but also like makes sense from a story POV.

00:41:27.120 --> 00:41:31.180
I guess I just wonder about like the punishing nature of the game and then to,

00:41:31.280 --> 00:41:36.980
to change what the game was and make it very punishing at the very end.

00:41:37.100 --> 00:41:39.700
Like it, I'm sure if you were able to make it this far,

00:41:39.700 --> 00:41:41.460
you're probably pretty good at this,

00:41:41.600 --> 00:41:42.500
but you know,

00:41:42.620 --> 00:41:46.240
you might not, it reminds me of other NES games where,

00:41:46.900 --> 00:41:49.480
you know, if you don't know the level inside and out yet,

00:41:49.480 --> 00:41:53.180
you might just not be able to react fast enough to know that like,

00:41:53.640 --> 00:41:56.180
okay, yeah, so there's this center gate and then this is a top left,

00:41:56.360 --> 00:41:59.200
you know, like some people just like memorize that stuff years later.

00:41:59.580 --> 00:42:00.960
I don't know if you can have that here.

00:42:01.080 --> 00:42:02.240
And so like when you die,

00:42:02.760 --> 00:42:04.040
you go back to the checkpoint.

00:42:04.260 --> 00:42:05.560
Sure. But like, if you die three times,

00:42:05.660 --> 00:42:08.620
then you have to go back to the beginning of that level and fight the final boss

00:42:08.620 --> 00:42:11.360
all over again, except for without those precious power-ups,

00:42:11.360 --> 00:42:12.780
uh, it feels a little cruel,

00:42:12.980 --> 00:42:14.160
but it's a cruel game.

00:42:14.160 --> 00:42:17.200
So let's talk maybe a little bit more about the,

00:42:17.300 --> 00:42:19.120
the difficulty. Um,

00:42:20.680 --> 00:42:22.620
you know, maybe on like a general scale,

00:42:22.760 --> 00:42:24.820
like just for shmups in general does.

00:42:25.280 --> 00:42:26.640
Yeah, go ahead. I do have,

00:42:26.740 --> 00:42:29.040
sorry, I do have one before we like go too far past,

00:42:29.140 --> 00:42:33.560
I do want to like jump back to the difficulty of the boss battle specifically.

00:42:33.940 --> 00:42:38.520
Yeah. Because I thought that boss battles were well-designed and difficult,

00:42:38.520 --> 00:42:41.620
except for one major flaw that I found in most of them.

00:42:41.780 --> 00:42:44.020
And I think I got like a little more than halfway through the game.

00:42:44.140 --> 00:42:45.040
So maybe they get better,

00:42:45.060 --> 00:42:51.420
but almost every boss I beat was by finding a pretty obvious spot that I wouldn't get hit

00:42:51.420 --> 00:42:53.860
and just standing there and shooting like,

00:42:54.060 --> 00:42:56.200
and not moving because the patterns,

00:42:56.200 --> 00:42:57.160
at least one of those.

00:42:57.340 --> 00:42:59.300
Yeah. The patterns for these,

00:42:59.400 --> 00:43:01.120
it's like, it's not like other patterns was like,

00:43:01.180 --> 00:43:01.980
Oh, they're going to shoot this,

00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:05.000
this time. And then they're going to shoot three and then they're going to shoot five,

00:43:05.020 --> 00:43:06.800
but it's always moving and everything's changing.

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:08.060
It's like, they're going to shoot,

00:43:08.440 --> 00:43:13.160
you know, 20 bullets right here while they're shooting five bullets right here and three things right here.

00:43:13.240 --> 00:43:14.260
And they're gonna do that over and over again.

00:43:14.260 --> 00:43:18.120
I'm like, okay, well, if I just stand in the spot that I can see none of those bullets are hitting,

00:43:18.700 --> 00:43:19.820
it'll never change.

00:43:20.420 --> 00:43:21.580
There were some exceptions.

00:43:21.580 --> 00:43:25.340
There were a couple of bosses that then started moving and then I had to like actually beat them legitimately.

00:43:25.700 --> 00:43:29.640
But most of the time I was beating these bosses by like finding the spot where,

00:43:29.640 --> 00:43:32.320
and it wasn't like, didn't even feel like like a cheese spot,

00:43:32.440 --> 00:43:33.500
like a lot of other things where it's like,

00:43:33.600 --> 00:43:37.960
